WEBVTT

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.900
There.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.460
The mitarashi's ready.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.230
How about you?

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.700
Yes, just about.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.240
The forecasts say it's going to get hot.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.240
Oh.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.930
Okay, I'll switch over to 
anmitsu and parfait, then.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.470
Thanks.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.310
Oh, look at the time.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.000
Where's Sui?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:49.650
Sui.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.150
Sui.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:01.190
All right, time to open Rokuhoudou.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:07.000
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.460
<b>"Welcome to Rokuhoudou Café"</b>

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.640
It's no use. I don't know how to make it work.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.340
Hello?

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.080
Oh, sorry.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.190
I don't have time right now.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.570
I'm going to be hiding out in my usual spot.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.380
Organic?

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.840
Yeah, no. I'm not interested.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.200
Okay. Bye.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.810
Today's Lunch
 A: Japanese-style Pasta with 
Beef and Green Onion
 B: Bamboo Shoots and 
Fava Bean Risotto

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.810
There's a shop <i>here</i>?

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.150
Wait, this is a café?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.500
<b>Rokuhoudou</b>

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.500
"Rokuhoudou"?

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.820
Welcome. For how many?

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.110
J-Just me.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.570
This way, please.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.840
Is something the matter?

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.640
No, it's just that it's so retro.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.090
I like it. It's nostalgic.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.850
Thank you.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.970
Pardon me.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.600
It's a plum petal.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.670
Wh-When did that get there?

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.930
There's one that's in bloom by the entrance.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.860
By the entrance?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.620
I'll be back to take your order.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.620
Oh, a plum flower, huh?

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:58.340
It's been getting warmer lately.
It might have gone into bloom quickly.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.360
Yeah, it's warm these days.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.150
The first spring storm will be here soon.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.460
It will.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:13.130
T-Toki-kun, what is that 
creepy, unplaceable noise?

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.350
Hah, well that is...

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:25.900
G-Gakes or gookies? No, that's too weak.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.370
But Japanese snacks...

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:31.410
Tsubaki-kun's moaning as 
he's making desserts.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.250
He seems to be struggling to come 
up with a new menu for the spring.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.050
But Tsubaki-kun's hobby is desserts and 
his sweet tooth is his special skill.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.870
He's like the king of snack tourism.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.440
I'm sure he'll be fine.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.220
An input doesn't necessarily 
produce an output, though.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.760
I'm sure Tsubaki-kun knows that, too.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.470
Shut up, Gure.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.740
Why am I the one getting yelled at?

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.880
Because you're the one talking 
nonsense about my hobby

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.230
being desserts and my sweet 
tooth being my special skill.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:02.450
But you're made of fifty-percent 
sugar, aren't you?

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.690
And what's the other half?

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:06.800
Y'know.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.360
Don't dodge my question, you king of BS.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.190
Whoa, that's awesome.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.660
Sui.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.630
Are you ready to order?

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.630
A latte, please.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.310
Understood.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:37.980
One latte.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:38.780
Gotcha.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:39.700
There.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.990
This has to be ready by...

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.690
Here you are.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.830
Thank yo—

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.250
Gure's special bunny latte art.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:05:59.920
Bunny? What?

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:01.750
Enjoy.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.210
Wh-What?

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.420
<i>I see...</i>

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.230
<i>They call </i>this<i> a bunny?</i>

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:14.830
<i>So this café sells by having hot guys.</i>

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.050
<i>What is this?</i>

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.400
<i>The milk's fluffy and lightly sweet.</i>

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.400
<i>It's got a hint of bitterness, but...</i>

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:29.870
<i>It's really good.</i>

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.410
<i>Even though it looks terrible.</i>

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.040
Looks like my cute bunny did the trick.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.520
Obviously not.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:55.510
New items
 Renew last year's mousse!
 Dango set
 Kusamochi -> red, white, 
green, spring-colors
 Customer preferences
 Western: Parfait
 Japanese: Kinako

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:57.220
All right.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:06:59.730
I've made up my mind.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:03.020
We're all going to come up with 
the spring menu together.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.750
It can be menu items or 
just simple gimmicks.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.530
Help me find something.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:10.850
Sounds fun.

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.730
So we just need to come up with ideas.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:17.710
A lot of customers are looking 
forward to seasonal menu items.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.540
I'd like to come up with something nice.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:22.390
All right, let's do this.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:23.460
Thanks.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.380
Today's Lunch
 Omurice

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.570
Good morning, Kinako.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.860
What do you think should 
be on the spring menu?

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.760
I see, meow.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:42.280
This part has to be more like...

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:47.900
Ah, I love the shape and color 
of the plates Toki-sensei makes.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.450
Mine are nothing like yours.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.380
That's not true.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.110
You're all improving quickly, too.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:57.420
It must be because you're such a good teacher.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.370
Toki-sensei has an eye for detail.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.830
Thank you.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.750
I know.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:06.990
The bowls that Toki-sensei made before 
will be perfect for the coming season.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:12.380
Koubai pink, Yurushiiro pink, and that 
one color that has your name in it.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.480
Tokiiro pink, right?

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:15.970
Thank you.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.310
I just happened to have been 
thinking about spring.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.160
That's great.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.930
Yoshino cherry white would 
work for the spring, too.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.730
The plum trees are blossoming 
beautifully in the front.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.190
Thank you.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.420
Oh, my. Allergies?

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:34.090
That's another spring feature.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.410
You don't don't need to show spring 
appreciation with bodily functions.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.250
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:53.120
Mini matcha parfait and nerikiri set.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.580
Thank you.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.630
The chopstick holder is so cute.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.020
Time to eat.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.450
<b>Spring
 </b>Dango
 Nerikiri
 Western
 Cake
Jelly
Parfait

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.450
<b><-- Done last year 
Sakura     Green
 Field mustard, new tea
 Butterflies
 Plum
 Bamboo shoots
 Wakana</b>

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:19.450
<i>It was a cherry blossom 
sweets plate last year.</i>

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.640
<i>There's no sense doing the same thing again.</i>

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:26.460
<i>And a lot of people don't 
like cherry blossom flavor.</i>

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:30.210
<i>It was popular as a set with Sui's matcha.</i>

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:33.030
<i>It'd be nice to have something with matcha.</i>

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.340
<i>There.</i>

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.600
Huh? Where's Gure?

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.090
About that...

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:43.910
There's been a mistake, and 
the rice hasn't arrived yet.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:45.830
I asked him to go buy some.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.210
I hope he gets back in time.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.010
We may want to change the lunch menu,

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:56.990
knowing Gure.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:01.990
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:09:58.580 --> 00:09:59.940
Rokuhoudou.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:07.000
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:05.840
Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.500
Hooray for the rice.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.660
Grazie, grazie.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.000
Thank you.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.630
Good thing I took that shortcut.

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:19.010
No! No!

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.640
Sheesh.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.480
Hello, Gure?

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.770
<i>Tsubaki-kun. What's up?</i>

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.400
We switched to pasta for lunch.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.190
You don't have to hurry to buy rice.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.380
<i>Oh, really? Okay.</i>

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.270
Get back safe.

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:36.220
<i>Roger.</i>

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.240
Did he seem all right?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:39.870
I'm sure he's fine.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:40.700
He's Gure.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.830
No! No!

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:43.370
Listen to me!

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:47.370
I don't want to walk!

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:49.000
All right.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.630
So high!

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.180
Don't give your mom too much trouble.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:10:59.000
Okay!

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.950
Thank you so much.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:06.270
I just did what anyone would do.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.470
Oh, this isn't really much of a gift, but...

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:10.720
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:11.940
Here.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.940
Sakuramochi.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:15.710
Mamma mia!

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.940
Huge news!

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:28.380
Tsubaki-kun!

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:29.370
This is big!

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:34.540
Huh, what's with this chill vibe?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.630
We just survived lunch, 
so we're taking a break.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:40.170
So, what's this "huge news"?

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:41.610
Oh, right.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.390
This might be a shock, but stay calm.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.180
Apparently this is called sakuramochi, too.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:56.440
<b>Doumyouji

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:54.150
There are two kinds: 
Doumyouji and Choumeiji.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.420
It's fun how they're different shapes.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.440
You knew?!

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:02.610
Listen, Gure. You work at a sweets 
shop! You should know that!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.280
Do you think there's anything 
you could teach me?!

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:09.370
How long do you think I've 
been making snacks?!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.620
Sorry.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.750
So, is that all you've got?

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:19.800
Good work.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.970
What about you two? Any ideas?

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:28.000
I think it would be nice to have things

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.720
that'll make you think 
of the spring sunshine.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.140
Huh?

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.800
Were you going somewhere with that?

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.830
Would you like some more tea, Sui?

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.570
Thank you.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.700
E-Er, um...

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:44.450
How about you, Tokitaka?

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:48.210
I'm thinking perhaps we can 
create a sense of spring

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.870
outside of the menu as well.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:54.500
That sounds good.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:13:00.490
I feel like I have an idea 
just waiting to pop.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:02.580
Pop!

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:09.760
That's not how you look at a friend!

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.920
<b>Plum                               White clover
Sakura cake?                      Japanese mugwort
 Chrysanthemum                       Strawberries
 Garland chrysanthemum           Bamboo shoots | Higashi
 Lily-of-the-valley                       New tea
Wakana</b>

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.220
Thank you.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:16.370
My stomach growls in the 
late afternoon, too.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.870
I-I see.

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.880
May I look at the menu?

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.460
Coming right up.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.200
Here you are.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:30.640
The ochazuke set.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:36.820
We use a kind of spring seasonal 
salmon called tokishirazu.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:40.570
The bamboo shoots and vegetables are 
organic, picked from the garden here.

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:43.650
Please enjoy it with this dashi broth.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.310
Organic vegetables.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.580
Enjoy your stay.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.590
<i>It looks nice and oily.</i>

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.480
<i>The ikura is sparkling, too.</i>

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.340
Time to eat.

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.260
<i>This dashi is so good.</i>

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.490
<i>I never knew rice could be so good.</i>

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.520
<i>This makes me want to try the 
other items on the menu.</i>

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:26.280
Excuse me.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:29.160
Could I have the mini matcha 
parfait and Japanese sweets set?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:30.460
Okay.

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.610
Thank you.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.900
Come back soon.

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:20.760
Did you like it?

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:29.420
Yes.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:30.760
It was delicious.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:35.930
It's so fragrant.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:42.390
This tea is good, too.

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:46.240
Please have more, if you'd like.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.650
You're using a different chopstick holder.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.070
May I have some more tea?

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:56.900
Sure.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:02.880
It's so relaxing.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:08.190
I really lose track of the time here.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:09.960
Please enjoy.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:15.230
It's the first time my project 
proposal went through,

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:16.770
but it's not going too well.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:21.040
I thought maybe if I changed my environment, 
I could be more productive.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.550
But then all the food looked 
so nice, I got distracted.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.230
I ended up spending my 
time eating and relaxing.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:33.570
I'm not sure what to say.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.070
Oh, no, it's my own fault.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.460
I appreciate it, though.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:45.150
I think of the shop itself 
as a kind of snack.

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:49.170
It's there when you want 
to take a break from work.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:54.110
It's a cup of coffee or a batch of sweets.

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.730
I believe we serve the same purpose.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.760
No one needs coffee or sweets to survive,

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:05.100
but they give you a little bit of relief.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.940
That's how I want this place to be.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.160
<i>That's what I've been aspiring to, too.</i>

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:20.530
I work as an event planner.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:32.540
<b>Meeting room            Partition
Table | Chair
White board

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:22.960
I'm trying to make something

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:26.900
that'll have the guests feeling 
genuinely happy to have come.

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:31.650
Something that isn't a necessity, 
but would add color to life.

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:35.550
That's the kind of event I want to make.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:38.800
That's a wonderful job.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.150
The event I'm planning right now

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:57.060
is to have people go cherry blossom 
viewing within the company.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.060
That's my job, and yet,

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:03.640
I didn't even notice there were 
flowers blooming outside the café.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:09.600
There's no way someone like me 
could show people a fun time.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:16.610
You noticed the next spring, though, ma'am.

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:20.320
You're the first to have noticed.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.930
Thank you.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:35.190
I'm going to quit work.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.210
You're quitting your job?!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.950
N-No.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:40.570
I'm changing my strategy.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.670
When I work, I work.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:43.950
When I rest, I rest.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:48.660
Here, I'm going to rest like hell.

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:50.540
Um...

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:51.920
Yes?

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:56.050
Sorry, I overheard you.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:20:00.170
Is it okay if we borrow your 
cherry blossom viewing idea?

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:02.450
Idea?

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:04.220
S-Sure.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.290
Thank you.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:10.260
Hello? It's me.

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:11.480
Do you have a minute?

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:16.980
Sorry for turning you down the other day.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.740
I found a good shop.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.820
Let's go together sometime.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:24.140
Hey, Tsubaki-kun, what was that about?

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:26.870
I just came up with a good idea.

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.370
They have makunouchi bentos!

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.370
That's interesting.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.910
There's so much variety. It looks fun.

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:40.680
You can have any of the dango 
in place of hanami dango.

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:43.790
You also have a choice of 
three different paper boxes.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.310
I recommend having it to 
go along with a latte.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.400
That sounds good.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.000
Let's go cherry blossom viewing with it.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.310
Sounds good.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.810
I'm going to buy one for Mom, too.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:58.230
<i>When you want to take a breather...</i>

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.090
Come back soon.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.240
<i>You have a place within arm's reach.</i>

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.700
Hey, guys, want to go 
cherry blossom viewing?

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.890
What? There's no way we're going 
to do that on such short notice.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:14.250
I've already checked on the best spots.

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:16.750
I bought sake and sheets, too.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:22.260
All we need is four makunouchi 
bentos, and we're all set.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.230
All right.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:26.780
I'll get some ready.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.030
It's settled.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:31.770
<i>You might not need it to live, but 
that makes life a little more cozy.</i>

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:35.300
Sweet! Time to party!

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:35.700
<i>That's the kind of place that we,</i>

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:41.500
<i>Rokuhoudou, aspire to be.</i>

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:18.110
Sui, have you heard of manjyu chazuke?

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:30.100
<b>Next episode</b>

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:30.100
<b>"A Teahouse's Secrets"</b>

00:23:18.110 --> 00:23:21.070
The chazuke that Mori Ougai 
is said to have liked?

00:23:21.070 --> 00:23:25.370
I drew on that to make this manju omusubi.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:30.100
<b>Come again soon.</b>

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.340
Watch what happens when 
you pour sencha on top.
